meta {
  name: Create Session
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/internal/whalesync/sessions
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "whalesyncTeamId": "tm_abc123def456",
    "name": "Example Team",
    "liveExportAccess": {
      "paused": false,
      "recordLimit": 1000000,
      "fastestCadence": "daily"
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Ensure the team's shadow user exists and mint a 10-minute session token for it.
  Idempotent on `whalesyncTeamId`: any member's session reaches the same shadow user.
  Returns { scratchUserId, apiToken, expiresAt }.

  A missing shadow user is created as a pure one (clerkId `ws_<whalesyncTeamId>`, `name`
  as its label, no email); an existing one's name is left alone. `name` and
  `liveExportAccess` are optional: the session applies the team's Live Export access as
  Set Live Export Access does, and without one an existing plan is left alone and a new
  one runs with no limits. The old `subscription` payload is still accepted and mapped
  onto an access. Unknown body keys are stripped, not rejected. Returns 409 when the user
  holding the team id is a real Scratch account.
}
